Cascade — third-party license report
=====================================

This file lists every third-party Go module in cascade's dependency graph and
its license, as reported by `go-licenses` against the full module graph
(`go list -m all`). It excludes github.com/acamarata/cascade itself (this
module, not a third party).

Generated by the release pipeline (.goreleaser.yaml `before.hooks`, per
12-QUALITY-CONSTITUTION.md Art.10.1 which re-homes THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES from
repo root to docs/) from the module graph at release time, taking the UNION
across every release GOOS (R-14.1 matrix: darwin, linux, windows) since some
dependencies are platform-conditional (see mousetrap note below). Regenerate
locally with:

    for goos in darwin linux windows; do
      GOOS=$goos go-licenses csv ./... 2>/dev/null
    done | grep -v '^github.com/acamarata/cascade,' | sort -u

Module                                 License        Source
--------------------------------------- -------------- ------------------------------------------------------------------
github.com/pelletier/go-toml/v2        MIT            https://github.com/pelletier/go-toml/blob/v2.4.3/LICENSE
github.com/inconshreveable/mousetrap   Apache-2.0     https://github.com/inconshreveable/mousetrap/blob/v1.1.0/LICENSE
github.com/spf13/cobra                 Apache-2.0     https://github.com/spf13/cobra/blob/v1.10.2/LICENSE.txt
github.com/spf13/pflag                 BSD-3-Clause   https://github.com/spf13/pflag/blob/v1.0.9/LICENSE

This list is scoped to modules actually IMPORTED by cascade's own packages
across the release GOOS matrix (the go-licenses default: `go list -deps`
transitive closure of compiled code), which is what ships inside the
binaries. github.com/inconshreveable/mousetrap is imported by spf13/cobra
ONLY on GOOS=windows (cobra's windows "double-click" detection) — it does
not appear under darwin/linux go-licenses runs, which is why the union across
all three release GOOSes, not a single-platform run, is required. go.yaml.in/
yaml/v3 and gopkg.in/check.v1 are test-only transitive dependencies of
pelletier/go-toml and are never compiled into any cascade binary on any release
platform. All four remain in go.sum (required to build/test the module
graph); the latter two are intentionally absent from this report, which
documents what actually ships, not the full go.sum.

Per .claude/rules/dependency-rules.md (acamarata dependency policy, applies
project-wide): only MIT, BSD-2/3-Clause, Apache-2.0, ISC, and CC0 licenses are
accepted for cascade's own dependencies. GPL/LGPL/AGPL/SSPL are blocked. All
entries above satisfy that policy.
